-- non-destructive rollback marker for migration 33
--
-- Migration 33 repairs databases that already recorded migration 32. The
-- corrected migration 32 owns these same canonical fields and indexes, so a
-- version rollback must not remove them or recreate the unsafe global trust
-- identity. This statement makes the discovered down migration explicit while
-- preserving the canonical v32 schema, backfilled keys, and link resolution.

RETURN { migration: 33, schema_preserved: true };
